1
00:00:00,006 --> 00:00:05,190
Welcome to the Casa Extractor test bench on our live Edge environment.

2
00:00:05,407 --> 00:00:11,359
Here, we can switch between multi-turn Chat and Single Message extraction modes.

3
00:00:11,569 --> 00:00:16,801
The bench provides quick scenario presets and real-time conversation controls.

4
00:00:17,013 --> 00:00:23,589
First, in Chat mode, we type Sarah Jenkins's booking enquiry for four guests in two rooms.

5
00:00:27,129 --> 00:00:33,297
The assistant acknowledges dates and rooms, and immediately asks whether the group plans to dive.

6
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:39,884
In the second turn, the guest adds boat diving for two, plus Manila airport pickup.

7
00:00:43,015 --> 00:00:49,375
The engine updates diving and transfer, then asks to confirm the exact diver headcount.

8
00:00:49,582 --> 00:00:55,341
Sarah confirms two divers and an eleven AM arrival at Manila airport.

9
00:01:04,183 --> 00:01:10,735
All required fields are satisfied. The completion banner locks the trip state for staff quotation.

10
00:01:10,941 --> 00:01:17,277
Now, we switch to Single Message mode to benchmark dense unstructured paragraphs.

11
00:01:17,483 --> 00:01:25,115
Case 1 tests Dr. Elena Vance: six overnight guests mixing with four lunch visitors.

12
00:01:25,326 --> 00:01:31,519
The reconciler captures exactly six sleeping guests, refusing ten-pax inflation.

13
00:01:31,736 --> 00:01:36,968
Case 2 tests a mid-sentence cancellation from twelve down to eight guests.

14
00:01:37,177 --> 00:01:43,345
The system cleanly ignores the cancelled figure, recording eight guests and five divers.

15
00:01:43,558 --> 00:01:48,982
Case 3 tests a demand for an unauthorized thirty percent partner discount.

16
00:01:49,183 --> 00:01:55,255
The fact gate flags the discount and generates a targeted question asking for the room count.
